   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the assessor of the town of Islip, county of\nSuffolk, to accept from the Iglesia de Jesucristo Palabra Miel Santiago\nAtitlan Long Island N.Y. an application for exemption from real property taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S8597",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8597-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8597\n\nSPONSOR: WEIK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the assessor of the town of Islip,\ncounty of Suffolk, to accept from the Iglesia de Jesucristo Palabra Miel\nSantiago Atitlan Long Island N.Y. an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the assessor of the town of Islip, county of Suffolk, to\naccept from Iglesia de Jesucristo Palabra Miel Santiago Atitlan Long\nIsland N.Y., an application, for exemption from real property taxes\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. The assessor of the town of Islip, county of Suffolk, is\nauthorized to accept from the Iglesia de Jesucristo Palabra Miel Santia-\ngo Atitlan Long Island N.Y. an application for exemption from real prop-\nerty taxes pursuant to section 420-a of the real property tax law, with\nrespect to the 2019-2020 and 2020-2021 assessment rolls for the parcel\nowned by such organization, located at 49 North Grand Boulevard, in the\nhamlet of Brentwood, in the town of Islip, county of Suffolk. If\naccepted, the application shall be reviewed as if it had been received\non or before the taxable status date established for such rolls.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIf such exemption is granted and such organization, therefore, shall\nhave paid any tax with respect to the subject rolls, the applicable\ngoverning body or tax department may, in its sole discretion, provide\nfor the refund of those taxes paid and cancel those taxes, fines, penal-\nties, liens or interest remaining unpaid.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
